  "reason": "With no prior experiments, there is no evidence to exploit, so the priority is establishing a clear, low-cost baseline to anchor all future comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the design space: it uses a standard, well-understood linear encoder (PCA to 2000 dims) on a single RNA profile, avoiding confounds from multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders, image processing, or fusion. This gives a fast, reliable reference for RNA-only performance. Subsequent experiments can then isolate the marginal contribution of each design axis (multiprofile + aggregation, alternative RNA encoders, image modality, multimodal fusion) by holding other factors constant relative to this baseline. Choosing the simplest baseline first maximizes information per experiment because every later result can be interpreted as a delta from this reference, and it is computationally cheap, preserving budget for more complex configurations later."
}

